# Stitch select chevron lock (hard — permanent)

## The chronic bug

Filter `<select>`s show a garbled `~` / double-∨ when **both** are active:

1. Tailwind Forms **SVG** `background-image` on the select, **and**
2. A Material Symbols sibling `<span class="material-symbols-outlined">expand_more</span>`

Agents keep “fixing” one screen with a one-off `background-image: none` — then the next screen regresses.

## Permanent contract

1. **Shared kill** lives in `kentender_core/public/css/kt_stitch_desk_chrome.css`:

   `select:has(+ .material-symbols-outlined) { background-image: none !important; }`

   Scoped under `.kt-stitch-canvas` / `.kt-str-root` / `.kt-bud-root`. Do **not** remove this rule.

2. Module utility sheets that paint the SVG Forms chevron (Strategy/Budget) must include the same `:has(+ .material-symbols-outlined)` kill **immediately after** the SVG rule (load-order belt).

3. **Never** re-scope Budget CSS onto `.kt-str-root` (or Strategy CSS onto `.kt-bud-root`) for select chevrons — cross-module bleed re-stacks glyphs.

4. Page-size footer selects use Material only — already pinned in `kt_stitch_table_footer.css`.

## When adding a new Stitch filter bar

- Prefer Material `expand_more` sibling (portfolio / Downstream pattern) **or** SVG-only (Budget portfolio). Not both.
- If Material sibling is present, do not add per-screen SVG; the `:has` rule covers it.
- Gate markers: `kentender_core.stitch_desk_chrome_registry.REQUIRED_SHARED_CSS_MARKERS` must keep `select:has(+ .material-symbols-outlined)`.
- Playwright: `assertStitchDeskChrome` fails if Material sibling + non-`none` background-image.

## Disallowed

- Deleting the `:has()` kill “because portfolio already sets none”.
- Copy-pasting Strategy select SVG rules into Budget utilities targeting `.kt-str-root`.
- Claiming UI Done with garbled filter chevrons on any Stitch Desk surface.
